      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil+\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil\\), we need to evaluate each term separately and then sum the results.\n\n1. **Evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\sqrt{2.25} = 1.5\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of 1.5 is 2 because the ceiling function rounds up to the nearest integer.\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil1.5\\right\\rceil = 2\n   \\]\n\n2. **Evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\frac{9}{4} = 2.25\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of 2.25 is 3 because the ceiling function rounds up to the nearest integer.\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil2.25\\right\\rceil = 3\n   \\]\n\n3. **Evaluate \\(\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil\\):**\n   \\[\n   \\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2 = \\frac{81}{16} = 5.0625\n   \\]\n   The ceiling of 5.0625 is 6 because the ceiling function rounds up to the nearest integer.\n   \\[\n   \\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil5.0625\\right\\rceil = 6\n   \\]\n\nNow, we sum the results of the three ceiling functions:\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil + \\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil + \\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 2 + 3 + 6 = 11\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{11}\n\\]",
