      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "Starting from the innermost parentheses, we first deal with $\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2$:\n\n\\[\n\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2 = \\frac{81}{16}\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil\\frac{81}{16}\\right\\rceil = 5\n\\]\n\nNow, let's continue on. We have $\\frac{9}{4} = 2.25$, so:\n\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil2.25\\right\\rceil = 3\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to evaluate the square root part:\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}} = \\sqrt{2.25} = 1.5\n\\]\n\nThus,\n\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil = \\left\\lceil1.5\\right\\rceil = 2\n\\]\n\nPutting all together, we have:\n\n\\[\n\\left\\lceil\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{4}}\\right\\rceil + \\left\\lceil\\frac{9}{4}\\right\\rceil + \\left\\lceil\\left(\\frac{9}{4}\\right)^2\\right\\rceil = 2 + 3 + 5\n\\]\n\nAdding these values:\n\n\\[\n2 + 3 + 5 = 10\n\\]\n\nTherefore,\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10}\n\\]",
